//! @yah:handoff("(1b) WHY IT NEVER CAME BACK — THE ACTUAL ROOT CAUSE, and it is STILL FIRING every ~2 minutes as of 20:19 UTC. `journalctl -u yubaba` on us-south-001 (node_id 1, the current raft leader): `WARN kamaji refused the headscale appliance (kamaji deploy_workload: kamaji error: BackendRefused: workload headscale declares yah.durability.tier = \"stream\" but this kamaji has no hydrate helper configured — start it with --hydrate-helper PATH (or set KAMAJI_HYDRATE_HELPER). Starting without one would bring the workload up against an empty volume, which looks exactly like a healthy first boot) — reverting to the headscale.service systemd unit`. The fallback then also fails: `systemctl[...]: Failed to enable unit: Unit headscale.service does not exist`. Yubaba concludes `ERROR APPLIANCE UNHEALTHY: elected owner could not start the appliance and has NOT claimed ownership: no start path succeeded (kamaji: ...; systemd: \\`systemctl enable --now headscale\\` failed — unit missing or systemd unavailable)` with round_exhausted:true, then `headscale appliance torn down on leadership loss` / `headscale stopped on leadership loss`, then loops. Between retry rounds it logs `ERROR APPLIANCE UNHEALTHY: no eligible candidate can run the appliance — the cluster has no coordinator and is not silently carrying on` every 10s. Same shape at 06:45-06:48 and at 20:18:24 — 13.7 hours of identical failure. (Side note: us-west-001's `systemctl is-active headscale` = `inactive` cited in the ticket is meaningless — the unit does not exist on any node; headscale is a kamaji native-exec workload, never a systemd unit.)")
