//! @yah:handoff("(1d) THIS EXACT FAILURE WAS PREDICTED IN WRITING AND THE SEQUENCE WAS NOT HONOURED. oss/yubaba/crates/cloud/templates/mirror.yml:90-96 reads: \"SEQUENCING HAZARD, still live: the moment ANY workload spec declares a `yah.durability.tier`, kamaji REFUSES to deploy it on a node whose kamaji has neither helper configured (kamaji-bin/src/hydrate.rs:170-178, src/tail.rs). A release carrying these binaries + the env vars below MUST reach every candidate node BEFORE the release that adds the declaration to headscale's WorkloadSpec, or the first roll of the second refuses to deploy the coordinator.\" mirror.yml:112-115 and :122-123 are the cloud-init steps that copy turso-backup-hydrate / turso-backup-tail and write the 50-durability-helpers.conf drop-in — and every one of them is guarded by `[ -f ... ] && ... || echo \"absent from this tarball...\"`, i.e. they SILENTLY NO-OP when the tarball lacks the helpers. That is why the declaration shipped and the helpers did not: the guard turned a missing prerequisite into a stderr line nobody read, and the next roll of yubaba took the coordinator down. This is the finding that should outlive the incident.")
